<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41918" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑπτά</span></b> , οἱ, αἱ, τά, indecl.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seven,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.421
			</span></i>, etc.; as a mystical number, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1093a13
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ἑ. νῆσοι</span> the
				<i>seven</i> largest islands, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				268
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				837a31
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἑ. θεάματα</span> the
				<u>Seven</u> Wonders, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.1.33
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2.11
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἑ. σοφισταί</span> the
				<u>Seven</u> Sages, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				15.109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.311
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἑ. σοφοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Stob.
					3.1.172
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἑ.</span> alone, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				1.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				286.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἑ.,</span> board of magistrates at
			Olbia, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				495.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἑ. ἄνδρες,</span>
			= Lat. <i>septemviri epulones,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				48.32
			</span></i>. (I.-<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>sept[macutenull],</i> cf. Skt. <i>saptá,</i>
			Lat. <i>septem</i> (fancifully connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σέβομαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				43
			</span></i>) : <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεπτά,</span> i.e. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηεπτά.</span>)</div>
